# Applies to builds whose context is the repository root. Only demo/chat.Dockerfile builds that
# way (backend/ and dashboard/ are their own contexts, and deploy/huggingface/push_space.py
# stages its own folder), so this lists what that image copies and leaves out everything else.
#
# An allowlist rather than a list of exclusions: the root holds .env with the real keys,
# ./models (the 1.2 GB model cache), node_modules, the SQLite files and the .git folder, and
# none of them may end up in the build context. A new file the chat image needs has to be
# added here as well as to the Dockerfile; the build fails loudly if it is missing.
**

!backend/constraints.txt
!backend/app/__init__.py
!backend/app/services/__init__.py
!backend/app/services/grounding.py
!demo/chat.Dockerfile
!demo/requirements-chat.txt
!demo/chat_server.py
!demo/chat_providers.py
!demo/chat_guard.py
!demo/workflows/__init__.py
!demo/workflows/retrieval.py
!sdk/src/

# Not even inside the allowed folders.
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
